[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/dialogue/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"lane_mab"
text = "# DRAFT
# Mab by the abbey gate at dusk, nights 1 to 6. She sees who comes and goes, nobody asks her, and she never eats the abbey's bread: the porter's reality check.
# Alms once a night (mab_alms_<night>): a heel of Fenchurch Street bread for him, and a little trust. Greets him warmly at trust 30, coldly below 0.
# Her own flags: lane_mab_<night> (talked to her tonight), lane_mab_bread, lane_mab_n<night>_<topic> (asked).
== start
-> start_known [if talked_n0_mab]
-> start_new

== start_known
Mab: Brother porter. So they let you in after all.
-> tonight

== start_new
(A woman sits against the wall by the gate, a clapper in her lap, her face wrapped to the eyes.)
Mab: Alms, porter? Stand off a little. I'm Mab. I'm always here.
-> tonight

== again
-> back [if night=1] [if lane_mab_1]
-> back [if night=2] [if lane_mab_2]
-> back [if night=3] [if lane_mab_3]
-> back [if night=4] [if lane_mab_4]
-> back [if night=5] [if lane_mab_5]
-> back [if night=6] [if lane_mab_6]
-> hello

== again_warm
-> back [if night=1] [if lane_mab_1]
-> back [if night=2] [if lane_mab_2]
-> back [if night=3] [if lane_mab_3]
-> back [if night=4] [if lane_mab_4]
-> back [if night=5] [if lane_mab_5]
-> back [if night=6] [if lane_mab_6]
-> hello_warm

== again_cold
-> back [if night=1] [if lane_mab_1]
-> back [if night=2] [if lane_mab_2]
-> back [if night=3] [if lane_mab_3]
-> back [if night=4] [if lane_mab_4]
-> back [if night=5] [if lane_mab_5]
-> back [if night=6] [if lane_mab_6]
-> hello_cold

== hello
Mab: Porter.
-> tonight

== hello_warm
(She lifts the clapper and knocks it once, softly, like a greeting.)
Mab: There's my porter.
-> tonight

== hello_cold
(She doesn't look up when you come.)
Mab: Porter.
-> tonight

== back
Mab: Still here? I'm not going anywhere, porter.
-> ask

== tonight
-> n1 [if night=1]
-> n2 [if night=2]
-> n3 [if night=3]
-> n4 [if night=4]
-> n5 [if night=5]
-> n6 [if night=6]

== ask
-> n1_ask [if night=1]
-> n2_ask [if night=2]
-> n3_ask [if night=3]
-> n4_ask [if night=4]
-> n5_ask [if night=5]
-> n6_ask [if night=6]

== alms
(You drop a coin in the bowl at her feet.)
Mab: God keep you, porter. Here. Fenchurch Street bread, not theirs.
(She sets a heel of bread on the step between you, wrapped in a cloth, and draws back.)
-> ask

== bread [set lane_mab_bread]
Mab: Their bread? Never. Not a crumb, and I've been hungry enough to eat straw.
Mab: They hand it out at the gate on feast days. I give mine to the rooks.
Mab: Then the rooks sit on your wall and scream at nothing.
-> ask

# Night 1: his first night at the gate.
== n1 [set lane_mab_1]
Mab: Your first night at the gate. I'll be on this side of it, if you want me.
Mab: If you must turn a soul away, do it before the bell. The Keys takes them in till nine.
Mab: After that, it's the lane.
-> n1_ask

== n1_ask
* [if not mab_alms_1] (Give her alms.) [set mab_alms_1] [item mab_bread] [trust mab 5] -> alms
* [if not lane_mab_n1_watch] What do you watch for? -> n1_watch

== n1_watch [set lane_mab_n1_watch]
Mab: Faces. Who goes in, who comes out. Who goes in and doesn't.
Mab: You'd be surprised what nobody notices, porter.
-> n1_ask

# Night 2: about night 1. The knock with no one there.
== n2 [set lane_mab_2]
-> n2_knock [if n1_knock_no_one]
-> n2_saw

== n2_knock [note knock_no_one]
Mab: No one came to your gate last night. No one.
Mab: I heard the knock, same as you. I was looking right at the gate, porter. There was nobody there.
-> n2_knock_ask

== n2_knock_ask
* I believe you. [trust mab 10] -> n2_believe
* You must have dozed. [trust mab -5] -> n2_doubt

== n2_believe
(She's quiet a long while behind the cloth.)
Mab: Nobody's said that to me in eleven years.
-> n2_saw

== n2_doubt
Mab: I don't doze, porter. Not out here. Not at your gate.
-> n2_saw

== n2_saw
-> n2_merchant [if died_merchant]
-> n2_plain [if not n1_knock_no_one]
-> n2_ask

== n2_merchant
Mab: I saw your merchant go in. I never saw him come out. Then this morning they said the pond.
-> n2_ask

== n2_plain
Mab: Your first night done, and you're still standing. That's more than some.
-> n2_ask

== n2_ask
* [if not mab_alms_2] (Give her alms.) [set mab_alms_2] [item mab_bread] [trust mab 5] -> alms
* [if not lane_mab_bread] Do you eat the abbey's bread? -> bread

# Night 3: about night 2. What she saw in the lane; the rooks.
== n3 [set lane_mab_3]
-> n3_saw [if died_jankin]
-> n3_saw [if died_lane_death]
-> n3_quiet

== n3_saw
Mab: I saw it, last night. Under Gib's lantern, by the chandler's.
Mab: Tall. Taller than any man. It came from the corner of your wall, and it went back the same way.
Mab: Nobody's asked me. Gib's told it three times over, and Gib never saw a thing.
-> n3_tower

== n3_quiet
Mab: Nobody died in the lane last night. Something walked it, though. I kept very still.
-> n3_tower

== n3_tower
-> n3_rooks [if died_warner]
-> n3_ask

== n3_rooks
Mab: The rooks came off your tower before Matins, all at once, screaming. Before your bell, porter. Not after.
-> n3_ask

== n3_ask
* [if not mab_alms_3] (Give her alms.) [set mab_alms_3] [item mab_bread] [trust mab 5] -> alms
* [if not lane_mab_bread] Do you eat the abbey's bread? -> bread

# Night 4: about night 3. The little knock; Walter's bag; the pilgrim who went in by day.
== n4 [set lane_mab_4]
-> n4_child [if n3_child_knock]
-> n4_walter

== n4_child
Mab: You came to the grille last night and looked down at your feet, at nothing.
Mab: There was nothing there, porter. No child. No dog. I was watching.
-> n4_walter

== n4_walter [note incense_bag]
Mab: Walter came by with his bag. It smelled of your Matins before ever he reached your gate.
-> n4_pilgrim [if died_crypt_pilgrim]
-> n4_ask

== n4_pilgrim
Mab: And a pilgrim went in by day, yesterday. A man with a staff and a limp. I've not seen him come out.
-> n4_ask

== n4_ask
* [if not mab_alms_4] (Give her alms.) [set mab_alms_4] [item mab_bread] [trust mab 5] -> alms
* [if not lane_mab_bread] Do you eat the abbey's bread? -> bread
* [if not lane_mab_n4_fear] Are you frightened, Mab? -> n4_fear

== n4_fear [set lane_mab_n4_fear]
(A dry little laugh behind the cloth.)
Mab: Frightened? I'm a leper, porter. What's left to take?
Mab: Ask me again tonight.
-> n4_ask

# Night 5: about night 4. Three of them, by the mill race.
== n5 [set lane_mab_5]
-> n5_inside [if n4_mab=admitted]
-> n5_outside

== n5_inside
Mab: You let me in last night. Inside your walls.
(She looks at the bars of the gate, and doesn't touch them.)
Mab: I'll not go in again, porter. Not for bread, not for blessing.
Mab: Three of them, by the mill race. I saw what I saw.
-> n5_ask

== n5_outside
Mab: You left me out in that fog. I sat against your gate all night with my clapper in my lap.
Mab: Three of them went by, out by the mill race. Three, porter. I didn't breathe.
-> n5_ask

== n5_ask
* [if not mab_alms_5] (Give her alms.) [set mab_alms_5] [item mab_bread] [trust mab 5] -> alms
* [if not lane_mab_bread] Do you eat the abbey's bread? -> bread
* [if not lane_mab_n5_prior] Tell the prior what you saw. -> n5_prior

== n5_prior [set lane_mab_n5_prior]
Mab: The prior? He'd have me whipped out of the lane for a liar. Nobody listens to a leper.
Mab: Only you. And you're nobody either, porter. No offence.
-> n5_ask

# Night 6: about night 5. Roger's sergeant. Snow.
== n6 [set lane_mab_6]
-> n6_dead [if died_sergeant]
-> n6_lived [if n5_sergeant=admitted]
-> n6_snow

== n6_dead
Mab: The bailiff's man stood right there all night, calling at your grille. I told him to keep his back to the wall.
Mab: Then his lantern went out. I didn't see what came. I heard it, and that was enough.
-> n6_snow

== n6_lived
Mab: You let the bailiff's man in. Good. An hour after, something stood at your grille where he'd been, looking in.
Mab: It stood there a long while, porter. Then it went away up the lane.
-> n6_snow

== n6_snow
Mab: Snow tonight. It'll show me everyone who comes and goes. It'll show them me, too.
-> n6_ask

== n6_ask
* [if not mab_alms_6] (Give her alms.) [set mab_alms_6] [item mab_bread] [trust mab 5] -> alms
* [if not lane_mab_bread] Do you eat the abbey's bread? -> bread
* [if not lane_mab_n6_warm] Go somewhere warm tonight, Mab. -> n6_warm

== n6_warm [set lane_mab_n6_warm]
(Something like a laugh, behind the cloth.)
Mab: Where would a leper go that's warm, porter? I'll be here. I'm always here.
-> n6_ask

== leave
Mab: God keep you, porter.
"
